# Resolution
Fixed by `f78304b Make metadata pending slots durable for phase 9.2`.

The reissue path no longer removes the pending command and blindly calls
`next_metadata_command_id()` from the primary only. It now reads the primary max
metadata log index, scans the acting set max, and fails closed with
`MetadataCommandLogConflict` if a non-primary replica is ahead of the primary.
When reissue is safe, it computes the replacement command before mutating durable
state and replaces the exact primary `metadata_command_pending_slot` atomically.

Regression coverage was added with
`stale_duplicate_metadata_command_index_on_non_primary_fails_closed_without_dropping_slot`,
which proves replica-only duplicate log divergence does not spin and does not
drop the durable pending intent.
